  "about": "Massachusetts's inner borders, town by town: scripts/ma-shapes.mjs reads this, gives every town (or, for a town on a line, every part of it) to a shetach, smooths the borders between them (no town-line spikes or notches; owner, Nov 3: \"Why there be horrible pointy borders\") and writes data/shapes/ma-*.geojson, which data/shetachim.json claims. Change a town here, then run `node scripts/ma-shapes.mjs` and `npm run build`. Towns not listed go by longitude: west of `deren` is Connecticut's shetach (its own band claim, kept exact), between `deren` and `split` Central Massachusetts, east of `split` Eastern Massachusetts. Cape Cod and the Islands keep their three counties exactly. `exact`: shetachim whose town lines stay exactly as they are, not smoothed (owner, Nov 3: \"I liked the north shore borders\"); they keep their town claims in shetachim.json and the shapes round them are cut to them exactly.",
